    "text": "{\n  \"anomaly_detected\": true,\n  \"confidence\": 0.5,\n  \"anomalies\": [\n    {\n      \"category\": \"open_connection\",\n      \"components\": [\"U3\", \"C19\"],\n      \"pins\": [\"U3.28\", \"C19.1\"],\n      \"nets\": [\"Net-(U3-VCC)\", \"VCC\"],\n      \"observed\": \"The display controller's VCC pin (U3 pin 28) sits alone on the net Net-(U3-VCC) together with C19 (2.2u) pin 1. That net is not the board VCC net. The VCC net carries U3 pin 6 (VBAT) and U3 pin 11 (BS1) but not pin 28. The pin therefore has no supply connection; its only connection is a bulk capacitor to GND.\",\n      \"expected\": \"A supply input pin of the OLED driver should be tied to the board's VCC rail, with the 2.2 \u00b5F capacitor acting as a decoupling reservoir on that rail. The spec describes C7/C19 as a bypass on U4's VCC pin, which only works if that pin is powered.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(net (code \\\"22\\\") (name \\\"Net-(U3-VCC)\\\") (class \\\"Default\\\") (node (ref \\\"C19\\\") (pin \\\"1\\\") (pintype \\\"passive\\\")) (node (ref \\\"U3\\\") (pin \\\"28\\\") (pinfunction \\\"VCC\\\") (pintype \\\"power_in\\\")))\"},\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(node (ref \\\"U3\\\") (pin \\\"6\\\") (pinfunction \\\"VBAT\\\") (pintype \\\"power_in\\\")))\"},\n        {\"source\": \"spec\", \"quote\": \"`C7` (2.2 \u00b5F) \u2014 U4 `VCC` (digital-logic supply pin) to GND\"},\n        {\"source\": \"spice\", \"quote\": \"C19 Net-_U3-VCC_ 0 2.2u\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"If pin 28 is a required supply input for the display driver, the OLED logic/supply path is not powered from the board, so the display may fail to initialise or operate. The isolated 2.2 \u00b5F capacitor would only charge from the pin's internal leakage.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.5\n    },\n    {\n      \"category\": \"open_connection\",\n      \"components\": [\"U1\"],\n      \"pins\": [\"U1.1\"],\n      \"nets\": [\"unconnected-(U1-VBAT-Pad1)\"],\n      \"observed\": \"The STM32L476 VBAT pin (pad 1) is on its own unconnected net, with pin type power_in+no_connect.\",\n      \"expected\": \"ST's reference design connects VBAT to VDD when the backup-domain supply is not used. A floating VBAT pin is a known hazard for this MCU.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(net (code \\\"65\\\") (name \\\"unconnected-(U1-VBAT-Pad1)\\\") (class \\\"Default\\\") (node (ref \\\"U1\\\") (pin \\\"1\\\") (pinfunction \\\"VBAT\\\") (pintype \\\"power_in+no_connect\\\")))\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"The MCU's backup-domain supply is floating. This may cause RTC or backup-register issues or an unreliable power-on state, depending on the firmware.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.2\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The netlist shows the OLED driver's VCC supply pin (U3.28) isolated on its own net, connected only to a 2.2 \u00b5F capacitor and not to the board's VCC rail, which is likely a real open connection. The unconnected VBAT pin on the MCU is a weaker, secondary concern.\"\n}",
